WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.900
- So the district attorney, Bruce Castor,

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.730
decided to issue a promise to Cosby

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:06.870
that they weren't going to go
forward with prosecuting him,

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.240
and there is some controversy here

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.860
as to whether there is
an agreement or not.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.430
Cosby waived his Fifth Amendment rights

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:12.510
against self-incrimination

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:14.860
and gave four depositions
in the civil case

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.310
that Constand brought against him.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:17.570
The idea is that if the prosecutors

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.830
weren't gonna be able to
criminally prosecute Cosby,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.260
at least the victim could
recover civil damages,

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.390
which she was able to do.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.760
She won millions of dollars.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.030
And even in the civil case,

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.050
Cosby could've exercised
his Fifth Amendment right

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:29.460
not to incriminate himself

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.050
but he decided to give the depositions.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.040
The depositions included

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.110
all kinds of inculpatory statements,

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.130
including the fact that he gave Quaaludes

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.870
to women and then had sex with them.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.420
But that's only half the story.

